<title>USA: McDonnell bomb-guidance kit clears hurdle.</title>
<headline>McDonnell bomb-guidance kit clears hurdle.</headline>
<dateline>ST. LOUIS 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>McDonnell Douglas Corp on Tuesday said it received approval from the U.S. Air Force to begin low-rate initial production of the Joint Direct Attack Munition (JDAM) guidance kit.</p>
<p>The JDAM kit, when added to the tails of traditional &quot;dumb&quot; bombs, significantly improves weapon accuracy.</p>
<p>The first production lot of 937 JDAM kits are to be produced under a fixed-price contract value of $18,000 per unit. The kits are being developed under a $70 million joint U.S. Air Force, Navy and Marine Corps program.</p>
<p>((Reuters Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
